for my Game Of Thrones Bonus video I wanted

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.900
to talk about the Widlings.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.900
The show hasn’t spent a lot of time with
them this season, as of right now the Thenn’s

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.340
are the only new tribe we’ve met.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:18.420
So I’m going to do a breakdown of their
history and some of the more notable groups

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.420
up to this point on the show.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.021
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do Game of Thrones videos every week.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:26.160
Next week there’s a break, there won’t
be a new episode.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.920
So I’ll just be doing a bonus video.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.070
Be sure to subscribe to get it and feel free
to leave me suggestions for topics.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:37.030
Round 7 of the giveaway starts tonight when
I post my review video.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.140
So let’s talk some free folk.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.480
That’s actually what they call themselves.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.730
Like citizens of America call themselves Americans.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:49.010
The term wildling is like a racial slur that
people in the seven kingdoms use to describe

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.010
them.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:53.120
As in, they are wild.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:59.450
Ygritte spent most of Season 3 trying to dispell
Jon Snow’s preconceived notions about their

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:00.670
culture.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.960
The funny thing is that people north of the
wall also have a derrogatory term for people

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.260
south of the wall.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.770
They call them “kneelers”.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.070
As in they kneel to a king.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.709
Like Aegon the conqueror.

00:01:10.709 --> 00:01:15.159
So just because the people south of the wall
are super racist, doesn’t mean that the

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:17.749
Free Folk can’t also be super racist.

00:01:17.749 --> 00:01:22.450
There’s just a lot of racism going around
in a song of ice and fire in general.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.389
I like to think Jon was a pretty open-minded
guy, but the other high born people at the

00:01:26.389 --> 00:01:30.270
Night’s Watch like Janos Slynt are extra
super racist.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:35.490
The interesting thing about the Free Folk
is that yes, culturally they are a group of

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.849
people that adhere to a similar belief system.

00:01:37.849 --> 00:01:39.549
But in reality, they’re made of hundreds
of small tribes and clans.

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:40.549
Some larger than others.

00:01:40.549 --> 00:01:43.459
They’re like a patchwork society of people,
all with their own communities.

00:01:43.459 --> 00:01:48.119
Because life is so hard beyond the wall, those
communities tend to be pretty insular.

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:51.659
Which is why it was such a huge deal when
Mance Rayder united them.

00:01:51.659 --> 00:01:54.560
And not just them, he also got the Giants
to come and play.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.709
He is pretty charismatic, but really I think
he just showed them all a picture of a white

00:01:58.709 --> 00:02:03.029
walker and everyone collectively crapped their
pants and started running for the Wall.

00:02:03.029 --> 00:02:05.259
Where did there society originate from though?

00:02:05.259 --> 00:02:10.750
The oldest known inhabitants of westeros are
the The Children of The Forest, but they’re

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:17.830
a whole different race, the oldest human inhabitants
we know about are the First Men about twelve

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:18.950
thousand years ago.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:23.360
It’s totally possible there were other humans
in Westeros before that, but record keeping

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.820
didn’t really become a thing till the Andals
came and formed the seven kingdoms, which

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.520
was thousands of years after that.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.330
The Thenns, those cannibals we just me in
episode 1, consider their people to be the

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:35.200
last of the first men.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.561
Technically, everyone living in the seven
kingdoms is a descendant of the Andals, not

00:02:39.561 --> 00:02:40.700
the first men.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.200
But there’s a lot of interbreeding we can
talk about in a second.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.200
And quick side note.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.750
The Thenns, are actually not part of the Free
Folk.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.740
They’re actually a whole nation of their
own.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:55.730
The Free Folk are more like a free range group
of people like Craster, just living without

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.320
a real government or a single leader.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.790
The Thenns are a fully formed nation state.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.480
A pretty big one when you look at the map
here.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.730
The Free Folk kind of became an amalgam of
people who descended from the first men and

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:09.250
just migrated north during the Andal invasion
and people who were born in the south and

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:16.220
just didn’t want to live under the rule
of the King anymore.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:23.620
So when we first met Mance Rayder’s army
in Season 3, we were seeing core Free Folk.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:28.530
Like the free range communities, the Giants,
which are their own separate race, clearly.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:32.021
The Thenns, who we now know are also a separate
nation with laws and a leader called the Magnar.

00:03:32.021 --> 00:03:35.810
The show is playing with a lot of the distinctions
between the different groups beyond the wall.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:40.500
But generally all you need to know is that
Thenns are different from Free Folk are different

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.990
from Giants.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.760
The show made the Thenns cannibals too, and
that’s a small change from the books.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:51.870
The real cannibals were another community
beyond the wall called the Skagos the show

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.030
decided not to feature.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:58.959
Right now Mance is the King Beyond the Wall
because he united all of the biggest societies

00:03:58.959 --> 00:03:59.959
beyond the wall.

00:03:59.959 --> 00:04:03.710
He tries to downplay the term King, just because
not bowing to a king is one of their core

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.710
beliefs.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.280
But he’s not the first person to do it.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:13.050
There have actually been six people since
the wall was built to do it.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:17.542
A single person, or in one case two brothers,
united everyone in the north to try and get

00:04:17.542 --> 00:04:20.340
past the wall so they could invade the south.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:25.110
Which is funny, because it completely ignores
the real reason the Wall was built.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.901
To seal off the lands of always winter.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:33.650
Which you can see on the map here.

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:39.291
Not keep out the free folk living all over
the rest of the north here.

00:04:39.291 --> 00:04:44.389
Those other people living here at the time
even fought with the Children of the Forest

00:04:44.389 --> 00:04:51.090
and the other First Men to end the last great
battle with the White Walkers.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:58.319
Then the wall was built and over the centuries
the people in the south started to forget

00:04:58.319 --> 00:05:00.960
that the people in the north were their friends.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.909
And that’s when the term Wildling became
a racial slur and relations devolved to the

00:05:04.909 --> 00:05:07.639
point at which we’re seeing on the show
now.

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:09.520
Everyone has forgotten about the true threat.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:19.960
Everyone except Mance Rayder and a few other
people on the show.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:24.430
The most densely populated areas are naturally
in Thenn and the Haunted Forest.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:28.499
The further North you go the colder it gets
and even Free Folk have their limits.

00:05:28.499 --> 00:05:31.449
Crasters for example is the closest village
to the wall.

00:05:31.449 --> 00:05:32.710
If you can call it a village.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:34.629
And as of the events of Episode 6 this season.

00:05:34.629 --> 00:05:36.219
It no longer exists.

00:05:36.219 --> 00:05:41.289
Back in season 3 when Jon first met Mance
and saw his army they were up here in the

00:05:41.289 --> 00:05:43.330
Frostfangs.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:52.999
The raiding party we last saw in episode 3,
with Ygritte, Tormund Giant’s Bane and the

00:05:52.999 --> 00:05:56.379
Thenns was just directly south of Castle Black.

00:05:56.379 --> 00:05:58.759
So the raiders are attacking from the other
side of the wall.

00:05:58.759 --> 00:06:02.960
Which is a huge problem because there aren’t
really a lot of defensive positions on the

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:14.590
south side of 
the wall.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:22.900
After the Night’s King, remember this guy.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.589
Turned into a white walker and started enslaving
the other Night’s Watch brothers.

00:06:26.589 --> 00:06:30.129
He rebelled against the seven kingdoms and
turned the Night’s Watch into it’s own

00:06:30.129 --> 00:06:32.659
small kingdom for a little while.

00:06:32.659 --> 00:06:37.080
As a result, when he was defeated, laws were
passed that said the Night’s Watch could

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.930
never build defenses on the south side of
the wall.

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:43.020
So that if the Night’s Watch ever went bonkers
again in the future, they wouldn’t be able

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:46.949
to sustain a fortified battle against the
seven kingdoms.

00:06:46.949 --> 00:06:51.930
As an unfortunate consequence of that, if
the Free Folk attack them from the south.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.710
They’ll have a much easier time of taking
Castle Black.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:59.330
This is what we’re getting ready to watch
play out in the next episode.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:03.360
So cross your fingers that the rest of the
brothers listen to Jon Snow’s council.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:08.430
Because everyone but Sam and some of the new
recruits seem pretty ignorant.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:12.039
So what I’m really excited to see tonight
is what Jon Snow and the other brothers do

00:07:12.039 --> 00:07:13.500
to repel the raiders.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.590
And remember, this isn’t Mance Rayder’s
army, they’re a much much larger force that’s

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:16.960
still on the other side of the wall.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:22.379
The raiders are trying to open the gates by
the time Mance’s army arrives at the wall.

00:07:22.379 --> 00:07:26.469
So you have a small force here poking the
Night’s Watch at their weak point and this

00:07:26.469 --> 00:07:31.099
massive army on the other side getting ready
to flow through this little area.

00:07:31.099 --> 00:07:33.289
And they’re converging it at about the same
time.

00:07:33.289 --> 00:07:35.490
So this is all happening at once.

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.569
Be sure to send a raven to your loved ones.

00:07:37.569 --> 00:07:39.539
Because it’s going to be very very bloody.

00:07:39.539 --> 00:07:42.639
I’m really curious if they’ll do any more
cannibal jokes.

00:07:42.639 --> 00:07:43.639
But now it’s your turn.

00:07:43.639 --> 00:07:46.520
Let me know what you’re hoping to see in
tonight’s episode.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:51.419
I think we’re all crossing our fingers for
a “You know nothing Jon Snow” line.

00:07:51.419 --> 00:07:53.039
Ygritte is pretty pissed right now.

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:54.039
So we’ll see.

